========================================================================
Bundled third-party components
========================================================================

Binary distributions of PrismNext bundle the following third-party
components. Each remains under its own license, which accompanies the
component upstream:

* Electron — desktop application framework (MIT License)
  https://github.com/electron/electron
  Official installers are Electron applications and therefore include
  Chromium and Node.js as part of that framework.

* Tectonic — a modernized, complete, self-contained TeX/LaTeX engine
  (MIT License)
  https://tectonic-typesetting.github.io/
  Bundled as the default compile engine binary; the pinned release is
  recorded in scripts/tectonic-version.txt.

* PDF.js — Mozilla's PDF rendering library (Apache License 2.0)
  https://github.com/mozilla/pdf.js
  Viewer resources (cmaps, standard fonts, wasm, iccs) are bundled for the
  built-in PDF reader.

* TikZ catalog figures under
  `resources/teams/prismnext.core/skills/figure-tikz/library/` mix a
  vendored OpenTikZ slice (https://opentikz.org/,
  https://github.com/opentikz/opentikz) — templates, examples, and
  ml/systems icons, CC0 1.0 (see that directory's LICENSE-CONTENT) —
  with PrismNext templates under `library/prism/` (MIT). Brand marks
  inlined in a few OpenTikZ templates remain trademarks of their
  owners. Brand-logo icons are not shipped.

JavaScript dependencies are declared in package.json / pnpm-lock.yaml and
carry their own licenses; this NOTICE does not attempt to enumerate them.
